Interactive Tea Ceremony (OOP) — Project Plan

1. Goal
   Create an interactive console-based OOP system where the user provides parameters
   (tea type, temperature, time), objects simulate the brewing process, and the system
   outputs tea quality and guest feedback.

2. Architecture

2.1 Domain (Models)
    No input/output here.
    Classes:
    Tea (base)
    GreenTea, BlackTea (inheritance)
    Water
    Teapot
    BrewedTea
    Person → Host, Guest

2.2 Service (Logic)
    TeaCeremony
    Responsible for controlling ceremony flow and coordinating objects

2.3 Controller (Interface)
    CeremonyController
    Responsible for user input and displaying results

3. Core Classes
    Tea
    Fields: name, optimal_temperature, optimal_time
    Method: evaluate_quality(temp, time)

    Water
    Fields: temperature, volume

    Teapot
    Method: brew(tea, water, time) → BrewedTea

    BrewedTea
    Fields: strength, bitterness, quality

    Host
    Method: prepare_tea(...)

    Guest
    Methods: drink(tea), give_feedback()

    TeaCeremony
    Methods: start(), brew_phase(), serving_phase(), drinking_phase()

    CeremonyController
    Methods: run(), choose_tea(), input_temperature(), input_time()

4. Logic Rules
   temperature < optimal → weak tea
   temperature > optimal → bitter tea
   correct values → good quality
   Quality levels: bad / normal / good

5. Program Flow
    Start program
    User selects tea type, temperature, brewing time
    Create objects: Tea, Water, Teapot
    Brew tea using Teapot.brew() → BrewedTea
    Guest drinks tea
    Output tea quality and guest feedback

6. Minimum Features
    2 tea types
    temperature input
    time input
    quality calculation
    guest feedback

7. Implementation Order
    Tea + subclasses
    Water
    Teapot
    BrewedTea
    Quality logic
    Guest + Host
    TeaCeremony
    Controller

8. Expected Output Example
    Host prepares tea
    Brewing...
    Tea quality: Good
    Guest: "Well balanced taste"
